# THE GESTURE RECORDER (0.17.31; 0.17.44: it waits for a move): in the FX menu SEL + REC arms it; the first move of an FX knob (or an effect
# played) starts the writing, from that bar's start; SEL + REC again loops it from that bar's end, and the knobs play the loop. A knob turned
# by hand is the hand's again; SEL + REC while it plays lets all of them go.
seed 0
seamless 1
wait 2500
expect playing 1
tap FX
wait 100
press SEL
tap REC
release SEL
expect gesture 1
# armed: nothing moves, so nothing is written (it used to start at the next bar on its own)
wait 3000
expect gesture 1
# the crush (K2) up and back down: the first move starts it
spin K2 15
wait 100
expect gesture 2
wait 300
expect fxk1 >5
spin K2 -15
wait 100
expect fxk1 0
press SEL
tap REC
release SEL
expect gesture 2
waitfor gesture 3 6000
expect gsmask 15
expect gslen >15
# the loop plays the crush up again by itself
waitfor fxk1 >5 6000
expect gesture 3
shot gesture_loop.png
# the crush by hand: that knob is let go, the others still play
spin K2 3
wait 100
expect gsmask 13
# all of them let go
press SEL
tap REC
release SEL
expect gesture 0
expect gsmask 0
